---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/deliverability';
const title = "Diagnose recovery email delivery before increasing volume";
const desc = "Separate message eligibility, transport acceptance and inbox placement. A platform\u2019s accepted-send count does not demonstrate that a shopper saw the message.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">{desc}</p>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-12">
      <h2>Verify sender configuration</h2>
      <p>Google’s requirements for personal Gmail include SPF or DKIM for all senders, with SPF, DKIM and DMARC for senders above its bulk threshold. Bulk marketing and subscribed messages also need one-click unsubscribe and a visible body link. Consult the linked requirements for exact scope; these checks do not guarantee inbox placement.</p>
      <h2>Trace one failed journey</h2>
      <p>Start with the eligibility record: was the message suppressed, queued, rejected or accepted by the receiving server? Save the SMTP response and provider error category where available. Distinguish a missing event from an authentication failure, a temporary deferral and a hard rejection; each needs a different owner.</p>
      <h2>Keep suppression authoritative</h2>
      <p>Require complaints, unsubscribes and invalid-address decisions to reach every recovery sender. Do not import purchased lists into a recovery program or restart suppressed contacts during a migration. Set re-engagement policy around permission, relevant customer activity and actual sending history rather than a universal inactivity cutoff.</p>
      <h2>Handle changes deliberately</h2>
      <p>Before moving senders or adding volume, record the domain, authentication, audience source and existing baseline. Review receiver-specific failures and complaints as changes roll out. Pause the affected traffic when the evidence points to a configuration or audience problem; changing templates alone will not repair an invalid address source.</p>
      <h2>Evidence to request</h2>
      <p>Ask the provider to demonstrate message headers, unsubscribe processing, bounce classification and suppression export with your configuration. Use seed inbox checks as diagnostic observations, not a promise for all recipients. <a href="https://support.google.com/a/answer/81126?hl=en">Google’s email sender guidelines</a> are the primary reference here; other receivers have their own requirements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
